# Set `version` and `date-released` at each release, and add the Zenodo `doi:`
# once the integration mints one. Affiliation, ORCID and co-authors are still to
# confirm.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FluLens in published work, please cite it as below."
title: FluLens
abstract: >-
  A viewer and reviewer for influenza variant calls. It reads the output of the
  Flumina (Illumina) and FluPore (Nanopore) pipelines. It shows a run as samples
  by codons, one cell per call, coloured by allele frequency. It adds
  per-variant read-level evidence, strand-bias assessment, FluMut marker
  screening, nucleotide diversity and selection results.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hutter
    given-names: Carl R.
    email: carl.hutter@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/flu-crew/FluLens"
url: "https://flu-crew.github.io/FluLens/"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-03
keywords:
  - influenza
  - variant calling
  - low-frequency variants
  - genomic surveillance
  - visualisation
